WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.057
Welcome to this Seller University module on the Amazon Generic Product Policy.

00:00:05.057 --> 00:00:10.114
In this video, we'll help you understand the benefits of the policy.

00:00:10.114 --> 00:00:14.749
Learn how to create generic ASINs and resolve common error codes.

00:00:14.749 --> 00:00:20.649
The Amazon Generic Product Policy allows customers to easily differentiate between generic and branded

00:00:20.649 --> 00:00:21.070
products.

00:00:21.070 --> 00:00:26.127
Generic products are unbranded items that don't belong to an identifiable brand.

00:00:26.127 --> 00:00:29.920
An unbranded product does not have a distinctive name,

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:30.747
or logo.

00:00:30.747 --> 00:00:36.720
You can find the Amazon Generic Product Policy on the Seller Central Policy and Help page.

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:43.423
If you want to learn more about listing products, watch our video Intro to Listing Products in Seller

00:00:43.423 --> 00:00:43.760
University.

00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:50.320
Amazon Generic Product Policy helps customers differentiate amongst similar looking generic

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:50.757
products.

00:00:50.757 --> 00:00:56.880
By creating a new product with the brand name Generic or its local translation,

00:00:56.880 --> 00:01:01.760
you can ensure that other sellers won't be able to make changes to the product detail page

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:03.234
or add offers.

00:01:03.234 --> 00:01:08.640
This helps maintain consistency and clarity for sellers and Amazon customers.

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:14.240
To create an ASIN for a generic product without a universal product code,

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:21.040
UPC, global trade item number, GTIN, or other product identifier, you'll need to submit

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:24.105
a GTIN exemption to get approval from Amazon.

00:01:24.105 --> 00:01:28.320
In the Add Product tool, go to Catalog and click Add

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:28.720
Products.

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:30.320
Then select Blank Form.

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:35.120
In the Item Name section, fill in your product name and select

00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:36.876
the category and product type.

00:01:36.876 --> 00:01:41.440
In the Brand Name field, select the "This product does not have a

00:01:41.440 --> 00:01:42.753
brand name" checkbox.

00:01:42.753 --> 00:01:47.129
Next, select the "I don't have a product ID" checkbox.

00:01:47.129 --> 00:01:48.880
If an exemption is

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:53.285
required for your generic product, the button "Apply to Sell" will appear.

00:01:53.285 --> 00:01:55.120
If an exemption is not

00:01:55.120 --> 00:01:59.080
required, you will be able to continue on in the process.

00:01:59.080 --> 00:02:01.600
Click "Apply to Sell" and complete the

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:02.609
application form.

00:02:02.609 --> 00:02:05.637
Once you have finished, click Submit.

00:02:05.637 --> 00:02:08.160
You'll receive communication within 48

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:11.589
hours regarding the approval status of your request.

00:02:11.589 --> 00:02:14.160
When you receive your GTIN exemption,

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:20.000
be sure to wait at least 30 minutes before adding your product with the standard Add Product workflow

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:23.200
to allow our system time to identify your exemption.

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:26.400
One of the benefits of our generic product policy

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:32.640
is that it prevents unauthorized offers and changes to the product detail page to protect you and

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:33.308
other sellers.

00:02:33.308 --> 00:02:38.320
If you try to change a product detail page or add offers on another seller's

00:02:38.320 --> 00:02:42.501
generic product, you'll receive a listing error.

00:02:42.501 --> 00:02:47.280
To see solutions for error codes 5882, 5885,

00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:56.080
5886 or 5887, you can review our generic product policy videos for the specific error code you

00:02:56.080 --> 00:02:56.848
have encountered.

00:02:56.848 --> 00:03:01.840
You can find more information on error messages related to the generic product

00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:07.739
policy and the steps to resolve them in the generic product policy help page.

00:03:07.739 --> 00:03:08.160
Remember,

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:14.160
the Amazon generic product policy is designed to help customers easily identify and compare

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:15.063
generic products.

00:03:15.063 --> 00:03:20.480
By following the guidelines, you can create a better shopping experience for

00:03:20.480 --> 00:03:21.513
Amazon customers.

00:03:21.513 --> 00:03:26.160
Thank you and happy selling in the Amazon Store.
